(:adr
  :id "ADR-0079"
  :shortcode "D79"
  :title "Sovereign Single-Binary ASL Consolidation: Unifying Engine, Eval, Compiler, Evolver, and Memory into a Self-Contained Dependency-Free Executable"
  :status :active
  :date "2026-09-11"
  :cluster "architecture/runtime"
  :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
  :problem "The AgentScript toolchain currently suffers from fragmented separation across three components: asl-engine (resident daemon binary), asl-eval (evaluator binary), and asl/asl (a bloated 7389-line shell script containing an embedded 3319-line Python transliterator and ad-hoc string manipulations). Zero external dependencies on Python, Node, Rust, or third-party package managers; linking strictly to standard operating system libraries (system libc and macOS system frameworks), completely unifying engine, eval, compiler, evolver, and memory into a single sovereign executable (asl), while cross-platform Linux/Windows/browser execution is sovereignly decoupled via WebAssembly (asl-core.wasm under ADR-0078)."
  :drivers [
    "Single Sovereign Binary: Unify engine, eval, compiler, evolver, and memory into one compiled native executable (asl) under 300 KB"
    "Eliminate Engine Separation: Discard separate daemon and runner binaries in favor of a single unified executable supporting both resident server and CLI workflows"
    "Remove Bloated Script: Completely eliminate the 7389-line shell script asl/asl and its 3319-line embedded Python transliterator"
    "Zero external dependencies on Python, Node, Rust, or third-party package managers; linking strictly to standard operating system libraries (system libc and macOS system frameworks), completely unifying engine, eval, compiler, evolver, and memory into a single sovereign executable (asl), while cross-platform Linux/Windows/browser execution is sovereignly decoupled via WebAssembly (asl-core.wasm under ADR-0078)."
    "Isolate External Dependencies: Keep databases (SQLite, vector stores), WebGPU, and voice drivers strictly in separate pluggable modules"
    "Zero Gate Weakening: Preserve all 7 verification gates, dual-polarity assertion qualification, and 5-dimensional consistency audits"
  ]
  :decision "Adopt ADR-0079 (D79) consolidating all AgentScript runtime and developer tooling into a single native binary (asl). Integrate resident batch RPC, pure S-expression evaluation, AST delimiter balance verification, 7-tier gate execution, and 5D consistency auditing directly into the compiled executable. Retire asl-engine and asl-eval as separate binaries, prune the 7389-line shell script, and maintain strict physical separation for database and hardware drivers."
  :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D75" "D77" "D78" "D79"]
  :tasks [
    "Task43401"
    "Task43402"
    "Task43403"
    "Task43404"
    "Task43405"
    "Task43406"
  ]
  :consequences [
    (:pos "Zero external dependencies on Python, Node, Rust, or third-party package managers; linking strictly to standard operating system libraries (system libc and macOS system frameworks), completely unifying engine, eval, compiler, evolver, and memory into a single sovereign executable (asl), while cross-platform Linux/Windows/browser execution is sovereignly decoupled via WebAssembly (asl-core.wasm under ADR-0078).")
    (:pos "Replaces the 7389-line shell script with a clean, high-performance compiled binary (~250 KB)")
    (:pos "Unifies daemon, evaluator, compiler, and gate runner into a single executable interface")
    (:pos "Isolates database drivers and external adapters into separate pluggable boundaries")
    (:pos "Accelerates CLI cold-start invocations and verification gates from seconds to milliseconds")
    (:neg "Requires maintaining consolidated C99 unified launcher source until pure ASL self-hosting compiler pass")
  ])
